# Cell viability assay (MTT assay)

Previous studies shown that the nanozymes with peroxidase-like activity could generate strong oxidant.OH via decomposition of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{2}\) [49]. According to this phenomenon, we utilized Ni-hemin MOF nanocomposites for therapeutic treatment of cancer cells based on its efficient generation of \(\mathrm{OH}\) radical through the peroxidase activity. Therefore, to evaluate anticancer activity, we incubated various concentrations of Ni-hemin MOF \((7{-}60~\upmu\mathrm{g}\,\mathrm{mL}^{-1})\) with MCF-7 cells for \(12~\mathrm{h}\) . Firstly, inherent toxicity of nanocomposite was measured using MTT
